{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1PksQCfPo6rw8x1jKPU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SytnoWidDUvbBU69487uGY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py","offset":1,"limit":175},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1608,"cache_read_input_tokens":189648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1608},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c17c3a51-6084-4d41-893b-9946240d9b73","uuid":"d437ed00-09f7-4daf-b1c3-bf5a0d6ed6c4","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:22:55.446Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1Pks76CaUikgsUcWkK4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SytnoWidDUvbBU69487uGY":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py","offset":1,"limit":175}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SytnoWidDUvbBU69487uGY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\"\"\"\n2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n3\t\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t# PLAN-177 t2 (re-pass rc.4 P1-f). The POSITIVE half of the probe test.\n7\t#\n8\t# The S303 filter below identified a probe by ABSENCE alone — five governed\n9\t# markers missing — and absence is the shape of the events the ratio exists to\n10\t# find: a markerless real spawn (including one the PreToolUse hook admitted by\n11\t# failing open) was classified as harness noise and removed from the\n12\t# denominator. A probe-only window then reported green with\n13\t# `harness_probes_skipped=1` while the governance gap it was built to surface\n14\t# went unrendered.\n15\t#\n16\t# So the structural conditions are necessary, not sufficient: the row must ALSO\n17\t# carry the observed harness signature. The signature is CLOSED — the literal\n18\t# description the tool-materialization probe emits, anchored at both ends\n19\t# (`Load <Tool> via ToolSearch?`, S303 observation, prompt `noop`) — plus\n20\t# corroboration by `desc_hash`, which the emitter computes over the RAW\n21\t# description: if the two disagree the preview was truncated or redacted, i.e.\n22\t# not this short, secret-free probe line. Anything else counts. Every\n23\t# uncertainty resolves toward VISIBLE.\n24\t_HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE = re.compile(\n25\t    r\"\\ALoad [A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+(?:,[ ]?[A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+)* via ToolSearch\\?\\Z\"\n26\t)\n27\t\n28\t\n29\tdef _has_harness_probe_fingerprint(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n30\t    \"\"\"True iff the row carries the CLOSED, observed harness-probe signature.\n31\t\n32\t    Positive identification, never inferred from missing fields. An absent or\n33\t    non-matching `desc_hash` is NOT corroboration, so it returns False and the\n34\t    row is counted — the safe direction for an advisory that exists to expose\n35\t    unclassified spawns.\n36\t    \"\"\"\n37\t    desc = ev.get(\"desc_preview\")\n38\t    if not isinstance(desc, str) or not _HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE.match(desc):\n39\t        return False\n40\t    digest = ev.get(\"desc_hash\")\n41\t    if not isinstance(digest, str) or not digest:\n42\t        return False\n43\t    return digest == hashlib.sha256(desc.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n44\t\n45\t\n46\tdef _is_harness_probe_event(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n47\t    \"\"\"True iff the agent_spawn row is a harness-internal tool-loading probe.\n48\t\n49\t    S303: the ghost filter above was written for the ToolSearch probes of an\n50\t    older harness, whose Agent-shaped PostToolUse rows carried NO description\n51\t    (desc_preview == \"\" and desc_hash == SHA256(b\"\")). The current harness\n52\t    supplies a human-readable description for the same class of call — e.g.\n53\t    ``Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?`` with prompt ``noop`` and a fixed cheap\n54\t    model — so all four ghost conditions no longer hold and a pure\n55\t    tool-materialization probe lands in the denominator as a governance gap.\n56\t\n57\t    The discriminator is ``subagent_type``: the Agent/Task spawn contract makes\n58\t    it REQUIRED for every governed dispatch (``check_agent_spawn.py`` derives\n59\t    the authoritative archetype from it, and ``extract_skill`` Path D needs it),\n60\t    so a row that carries none was never a CEO dispatch. All five conditions\n61\t    must hold — no subagent_type, no archetype, no rail attribution, no\n62\t    ``## AGENT PROFILE`` and no ``## FILE ASSIGNMENT`` — so a real named spawn\n63\t    that merely lost one field still counts.\n64\t\n65\t    T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5/t7 P2): DEFERRED, not cured — this function\n66\t    ALWAYS returns False today and probe-shaped rows COUNT in the\n67\t    denominator (a probe-only window reads 1/1 red and the operator\n68\t    triages it). The former ``harness_probes_skipped`` counter was removed\n69\t    together with the exemption; no row is skipped, so nothing is\n70\t    \"reported through\" anything.\n71\t\n72\t    PLAN-177 t2 (P1-f): those five are NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. Absence is\n73\t    exactly the shape of the event this ratio exists to expose — a markerless\n74\t    REAL spawn, including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed\n75\t    open, matched all five and was deleted from the denominator. The row must\n76\t    ALSO carry the closed harness signature\n77\t    (``_has_harness_probe_fingerprint``); an unrecognised description counts,\n78\t    however markerless the row is.\n79\t    \"\"\"\n80\t    # Re-pass rc.4 t2 (P1): the S303 exemption is RETIRED until trusted\n81\t    # provenance exists. `desc_preview` and `desc_hash` are both derived\n82\t    # from the same CALLER-CONTROLLED description, so the hash corroborates\n83\t    # nothing: a real markerless spawn described as\n84\t    # `Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?` was silently deleted from the\n85\t    # denominator — the exact event this ratio exists to expose. Until the\n86\t    # EMITTER can stamp provenance the caller cannot forge, probe-shaped\n87\t    # rows COUNT (the conservative direction for an advisory: a yellow the\n88\t    # operator triages beats a green that hides a fail-open spawn).\n89\t    # _has_harness_probe_fingerprint is kept (tested) as the shape\n90\t    # DETECTOR for that future provenance-bearing emitter.\n91\t    return False\n92\t\n93\t\n94\tdef check_skill_unknown_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n95\t    \"\"\"Detect spawns that should have SKILL injection but didn't.\n96\t\n97\t    S94 follow-up: excludes intentionally skill-less archetypes —\n98\t    `general-purpose` subagent dispatches via the mitigated rail\n99\t    (ADR-082) by design have no SKILL.md anchor. They broker cross-\n100\t    LLM gate calls and similar utility work; counting them as FPs\n101\t    inflates the ratio to 100% during healthy Codex MCP sessions\n102\t    and trains the operator to ignore the channel.\n103\t\n104\t    A spawn counts as \"skill missing\" ONLY when its `archetype` is\n105\t    a custom (non-general-purpose) one AND `skill` is unknown/empty.\n106\t    That is the original PLAN-020 ADR-051 governance gap the\n107\t    detector was built for.\n108\t    \"\"\"\n109\t    # T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5 P2): DEFERRED, not cured. Both the S86\n110\t    # ghost filter and the S303 probe filter are RETIRED (absence-based,\n111\t    # caller-forgeable); every agent_spawn row counts until the EMITTER can\n112\t    # stamp provenance the caller cannot forge. The skipped counters were\n113\t    # removed with them — a permanently-zero counter reads as \"filter\n114\t    # active, nothing skipped\", which is the wrong claim.\n115\t    total = 0\n116\t    unknown = 0\n117\t    skill_less_by_design = 0\n118\t    test_pollution_skipped = 0\n119\t    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n120\t        if ev.get(\"action\") != \"agent_spawn\":\n121\t            continue\n122\t        if _is_test_pollution_event(ev):\n123\t            test_pollution_skipped += 1\n124\t            continue\n125\t        # T-2 deferred (t5 P2): ghost/probe exemptions RETIRED — the shape\n126\t        # detectors above stay tested for a future provenance-bearing\n127\t        # emitter, but no row is skipped on caller-controlled absence.\n128\t\n129\t        # Skill-less by design: general-purpose archetype dispatches\n130\t        # (mitigated rail per ADR-082) AND built-in subagent types like\n131\t        # Explore/Plan/claude-code-guide that have no .claude/agents/<name>.md\n132\t        # and so cannot carry a `Loads <skill> skill via reference` phrase\n133\t        # (drift-detector contract per S143 lesson). Adding them to\n134\t        # _ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL would violate the contract — exclude here instead.\n135\t        # S200: claude/claude-code-guide/statusline-setup are first-party\n136\t        # Claude Code built-ins (no .claude/agents anchor); counting them as a\n137\t        # governance gap is a false positive — exactly the FP class this filter\n138\t        # exists to prevent (else healthy claude-code-guide use trains the\n139\t        # operator to ignore the channel).\n140\t        _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS = {\n141\t            \"general-purpose\", \"Explore\", \"Plan\",\n142\t            \"claude\", \"claude-code-guide\", \"statusline-setup\",\n143\t        }\n144\t        if (\n145\t            ev.get(\"subagent_type\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n146\t            and ev.get(\"archetype\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n147\t        ):\n148\t            skill_less_by_design += 1\n149\t            continue\n150\t        total += 1\n151\t        if ev.get(\"skill\") in (None, \"unknown\", \"\"):\n152\t            unknown += 1\n153\t    if total == 0:\n154\t        msg = (\n155\t            \"no custom-archetype spawns \"\n156\t            \"({s} general-purpose, {t} test-pollution)\".format(\n157\t                s=skill_less_by_design, t=test_pollution_skipped,\n158\t            )\n159\t        )\n160\t        return \"green\", msg, {\n161\t            \"unknown\": 0, \"total\": 0,\n162\t            \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n163\t            \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n164\t        }\n165\t    ratio = unknown / total\n166\t    status = \"red\" if ratio > 0.10 else \"yellow\" if ratio > 0 else \"green\"\n167\t    return status, f\"{unknown}/{total} = {ratio:.0%}\", {\n168\t        \"unknown\": unknown, \"total\": total,\n169\t        \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n170\t        \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n171\t    }\n172\t\n173\t\n174\tdef check_hook_live_smoke() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n175\t    \"\"\"PLAN-082 Codex Item D replacement for hook_test_baseline."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c17c3a51-6084-4d41-893b-9946240d9b73","uuid":"8f3c0e01-ea23-4a80-81fc-093bfdf013aa","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:22:55.469Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py","content":"\"\"\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n\n\n# PLAN-177 t2 (re-pass rc.4 P1-f). The POSITIVE half of the probe test.\n#\n# The S303 filter below identified a probe by ABSENCE alone — five governed\n# markers missing — and absence is the shape of the events the ratio exists to\n# find: a markerless real spawn (including one the PreToolUse hook admitted by\n# failing open) was classified as harness noise and removed from the\n# denominator. A probe-only window then reported green with\n# `harness_probes_skipped=1` while the governance gap it was built to surface\n# went unrendered.\n#\n# So the structural conditions are necessary, not sufficient: the row must ALSO\n# carry the observed harness signature. The signature is CLOSED — the literal\n# description the tool-materialization probe emits, anchored at both ends\n# (`Load <Tool> via ToolSearch?`, S303 observation, prompt `noop`) — plus\n# corroboration by `desc_hash`, which the emitter computes over the RAW\n# description: if the two disagree the preview was truncated or redacted, i.e.\n# not this short, secret-free probe line. Anything else counts. Every\n# uncertainty resolves toward VISIBLE.\n_HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\ALoad [A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+(?:,[ ]?[A-Za-z0-9_.\\-]+)* via ToolSearch\\?\\Z\"\n)\n\n\ndef _has_harness_probe_fingerprint(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True iff the row carries the CLOSED, observed harness-probe signature.\n\n    Positive identification, never inferred from missing fields. An absent or\n    non-matching `desc_hash` is NOT corroboration, so it returns False and the\n    row is counted — the safe direction for an advisory that exists to expose\n    unclassified spawns.\n    \"\"\"\n    desc = ev.get(\"desc_preview\")\n    if not isinstance(desc, str) or not _HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE.match(desc):\n        return False\n    digest = ev.get(\"desc_hash\")\n    if not isinstance(digest, str) or not digest:\n        return False\n    return digest == hashlib.sha256(desc.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _is_harness_probe_event(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True iff the agent_spawn row is a harness-internal tool-loading probe.\n\n    S303: the ghost filter above was written for the ToolSearch probes of an\n    older harness, whose Agent-shaped PostToolUse rows carried NO description\n    (desc_preview == \"\" and desc_hash == SHA256(b\"\")). The current harness\n    supplies a human-readable description for the same class of call — e.g.\n    ``Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?`` with prompt ``noop`` and a fixed cheap\n    model — so all four ghost conditions no longer hold and a pure\n    tool-materialization probe lands in the denominator as a governance gap.\n\n    The discriminator is ``subagent_type``: the Agent/Task spawn contract makes\n    it REQUIRED for every governed dispatch (``check_agent_spawn.py`` derives\n    the authoritative archetype from it, and ``extract_skill`` Path D needs it),\n    so a row that carries none was never a CEO dispatch. All five conditions\n    must hold — no subagent_type, no archetype, no rail attribution, no\n    ``## AGENT PROFILE`` and no ``## FILE ASSIGNMENT`` — so a real named spawn\n    that merely lost one field still counts.\n\n    T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5/t7 P2): DEFERRED, not cured — this function\n    ALWAYS returns False today and probe-shaped rows COUNT in the\n    denominator (a probe-only window reads 1/1 red and the operator\n    triages it). The former ``harness_probes_skipped`` counter was removed\n    together with the exemption; no row is skipped, so nothing is\n    \"reported through\" anything.\n\n    PLAN-177 t2 (P1-f): those five are NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. Absence is\n    exactly the shape of the event this ratio exists to expose — a markerless\n    REAL spawn, including one admitted because the PreToolUse hook failed\n    open, matched all five and was deleted from the denominator. The row must\n    ALSO carry the closed harness signature\n    (``_has_harness_probe_fingerprint``); an unrecognised description counts,\n    however markerless the row is.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Re-pass rc.4 t2 (P1): the S303 exemption is RETIRED until trusted\n    # provenance exists. `desc_preview` and `desc_hash` are both derived\n    # from the same CALLER-CONTROLLED description, so the hash corroborates\n    # nothing: a real markerless spawn described as\n    # `Load WebFetch via ToolSearch?` was silently deleted from the\n    # denominator — the exact event this ratio exists to expose. Until the\n    # EMITTER can stamp provenance the caller cannot forge, probe-shaped\n    # rows COUNT (the conservative direction for an advisory: a yellow the\n    # operator triages beats a green that hides a fail-open spawn).\n    # _has_harness_probe_fingerprint is kept (tested) as the shape\n    # DETECTOR for that future provenance-bearing emitter.\n    return False\n\n\ndef check_skill_unknown_ratio() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Detect spawns that should have SKILL injection but didn't.\n\n    S94 follow-up: excludes intentionally skill-less archetypes —\n    `general-purpose` subagent dispatches via the mitigated rail\n    (ADR-082) by design have no SKILL.md anchor. They broker cross-\n    LLM gate calls and similar utility work; counting them as FPs\n    inflates the ratio to 100% during healthy Codex MCP sessions\n    and trains the operator to ignore the channel.\n\n    A spawn counts as \"skill missing\" ONLY when its `archetype` is\n    a custom (non-general-purpose) one AND `skill` is unknown/empty.\n    That is the original PLAN-020 ADR-051 governance gap the\n    detector was built for.\n    \"\"\"\n    # T-2 STATUS (re-pass rc.4 t5 P2): DEFERRED, not cured. Both the S86\n    # ghost filter and the S303 probe filter are RETIRED (absence-based,\n    # caller-forgeable); every agent_spawn row counts until the EMITTER can\n    # stamp provenance the caller cannot forge. The skipped counters were\n    # removed with them — a permanently-zero counter reads as \"filter\n    # active, nothing skipped\", which is the wrong claim.\n    total = 0\n    unknown = 0\n    skill_less_by_design = 0\n    test_pollution_skipped = 0\n    for ev in _iter_audit_events_since(24):\n        if ev.get(\"action\") != \"agent_spawn\":\n            continue\n        if _is_test_pollution_event(ev):\n            test_pollution_skipped += 1\n            continue\n        # T-2 deferred (t5 P2): ghost/probe exemptions RETIRED — the shape\n        # detectors above stay tested for a future provenance-bearing\n        # emitter, but no row is skipped on caller-controlled absence.\n\n        # Skill-less by design: general-purpose archetype dispatches\n        # (mitigated rail per ADR-082) AND built-in subagent types like\n        # Explore/Plan/claude-code-guide that have no .claude/agents/<name>.md\n        # and so cannot carry a `Loads <skill> skill via reference` phrase\n        # (drift-detector contract per S143 lesson). Adding them to\n        # _ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL would violate the contract — exclude here instead.\n        # S200: claude/claude-code-guide/statusline-setup are first-party\n        # Claude Code built-ins (no .claude/agents anchor); counting them as a\n        # governance gap is a false positive — exactly the FP class this filter\n        # exists to prevent (else healthy claude-code-guide use trains the\n        # operator to ignore the channel).\n        _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS = {\n            \"general-purpose\", \"Explore\", \"Plan\",\n            \"claude\", \"claude-code-guide\", \"statusline-setup\",\n        }\n        if (\n            ev.get(\"subagent_type\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n            and ev.get(\"archetype\") in _SKILL_LESS_BUILTINS\n        ):\n            skill_less_by_design += 1\n            continue\n        total += 1\n        if ev.get(\"skill\") in (None, \"unknown\", \"\"):\n            unknown += 1\n    if total == 0:\n        msg = (\n            \"no custom-archetype spawns \"\n            \"({s} general-purpose, {t} test-pollution)\".format(\n                s=skill_less_by_design, t=test_pollution_skipped,\n            )\n        )\n        return \"green\", msg, {\n            \"unknown\": 0, \"total\": 0,\n            \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n            \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n        }\n    ratio = unknown / total\n    status = \"red\" if ratio > 0.10 else \"yellow\" if ratio > 0 else \"green\"\n    return status, f\"{unknown}/{total} = {ratio:.0%}\", {\n        \"unknown\": unknown, \"total\": total,\n        \"skill_less_by_design\": skill_less_by_design,\n        \"test_pollution_skipped\": test_pollution_skipped,\n    }\n\n\ndef check_hook_live_smoke() -> Tuple[str, str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"PLAN-082 Codex Item D replacement for hook_test_baseline.","numLines":175,"startLine":1,"totalLines":536}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SytnoWidDUvbBU69487uGY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
